      "topic": "Short notes",
      "question": "Write short notes on the followings (any two): a) I/O processor; b) Vector Processing; c) Memory Interleaving; d) Loop Buffer.",
      "answer": "**I/O processor:** independent device-controller processor that executes I/O programs and transfers blocks with minimal CPU intervention.\n\n**Vector processing:** one instruction operates on whole vectors/arrays using pipelined functional units, improving data-parallel throughput.\n\n**Memory interleaving:** memory is split into banks accessed in overlapping cycles, so consecutive addresses can be fetched faster.\n\n**Loop buffer:** a small high-speed buffer holding recently fetched loop instructions, avoiding repeated instruction-cache/memory fetches.",
