      "topic": "Cache mapping and virtual memory",
      "question": "a) Explain different types of mapping technique used in cache memory.\nb) Differentiate virtual memory and cache memory.",
      "answer": "**a)** Direct mapping sends each memory block to exactly one cache line; fully associative mapping allows any block in any line; k-way set-associative mapping allows any block in one of k lines within a fixed set. Associativity reduces conflict misses at the cost of comparator complexity.\n\n**b)** Cache hides main-memory latency with small fast SRAM managed by hardware. Virtual memory gives each process a large logical address space backed by disk and main memory, managed by OS/MMU through pages and translation.",
