      "topic": "Pipeline hazards",
      "question": "What do you mean by pipeline hazards/conflicts? Discuss the different types of hazards being observed and also explain the possible solutions.",
      "answer": "A hazard prevents the next instruction from executing in its scheduled cycle. **Structural** hazards occur when hardware resources are oversubscribed (add more units or stall); **data** hazards occur when an instruction needs an unwritten result (forwarding/bypassing, stalls, compiler scheduling); **control** hazards arise from branches (prediction, delayed branches, flushing, branch target buffer).",
