      "question": "a) Describe Booth’s algorithm with suitable block diagram and flowchart.\nb) Show the steps of multiplication performed by using Booth’s algorithm of `7 × −5`.",
      "answer": "**a)** Booth’s algorithm inspects `Q0` and `Q−1`: on `10` subtract M from A, on `01` add M to A, on `00`/`11` do nothing, then arithmetically shift `A:Q:Q−1` right; repeat n times. A textual block diagram is `A / Q / Q−1 → adder-subtracter with M,−M → arithmetic shifter → control from Q0,Q−1`.\n\n**b)** With 5-bit operands: `M=00111`, `−M=11001`, `Q=11011`, `A=00000`, `Q−1=0`. After five add/subtract-and-ASHR cycles the final `A:Q = 1111011101`, whose signed decimal value is **−35**, confirming `7×−5`.",
