      "question": "a) Explain the difference between Hardwired Control and Microprogrammed control.\nb) What do you mean by horizontal and vertical microprogramming? Compare these two ways of microprogramming.",
      "answer": "**a)** Hardwired control generates signals with fixed combinational/sequential logic: fast but hard to modify. Microprogrammed control stores microinstructions in control memory: easier to design, extend and debug, generally slower.\n\n**b)** Horizontal microinstructions use one bit per control signal (wide, highly parallel, little encoding); vertical microinstructions encode mutually exclusive signals into compact fields (narrower control store but extra decoding and less parallelism).",
